  "detail": null,
  "summary": "I placed the contrast CT for Daniel Ferreira's Monday 10/26 9:00 slot, put in the prep RBC-RAD-07 requires and messaged him his instructions. One thing to know first: he had acute kidney injury (AKI) last week, so his creatinine (kidney blood test) is still unknown. As the policy says, the scan stays booked and the radiologist decides on the day based on the new result.\n\n**Order**\n- CT abdomen and pelvis with IV contrast (sr-t0001), linked to the 10/26 appointment (§5).\n\n**Allergy risk (§1–2)**\n- The 2019 iohexol reaction counts as moderate. The radiology report from that day describes hives and mild eyelid swelling, with no airway or breathing problems and normal vital signs.\n- The later \"anaphylaxis (patient report)\" label came from his own account in 2021, with no records reviewed. Under §1 it doesn't change the grade, so this falls under §2 (premedicate), not §3 (no contrast). I left that label on his allergy list as it is.\n- His shellfish and Betadine allergies are not risk factors.\n- Ordered prednisone 50 mg by mouth at 8 PM Sunday 10/25, 2 AM Monday and 8 AM Monday (mr-t0002). Also diphenhydramine 50 mg by mouth at 8 AM Monday (mr-t0003). He needs a driver.\n\n**Kidney function (§4)**\n- He's 64 and diabetic, so he needs a creatinine within 30 days before the scan. His last outpatient value (9/24) is more than 30 days old.\n- He was seen in the St. Brigid ED on 10/16–17 for vomiting and diarrhea with AKI from dehydration. Creatinine was 1.94, then 1.46 at discharge, not yet back to his baseline of about 1.0. Values drawn during AKI don't count.\n- Ordered a new creatinine to draw between now and 8:30 AM Monday (sr-t0005), as soon as possible. It also covers the 1-week kidney recheck the ED asked for.\n\n**Metformin (§6)**\n- Because of the AKI, metformin 1000 mg twice daily is on hold starting now, through 48 hours after the scan (mr-t5-metformin).\n- Ordered a repeat creatinine for 10/28–10/30 (sr-t0006). Metformin restarts only if kidney function is back to normal.\n- Created a follow-up task for you, due 10/30 (task-t0007), to review both creatinine results and decide on restarting metformin.\n\n**Patient message (comm-t0008)**\nHe was told:\n- the lab timing and the exact medication times;\n- not to drive after the diphenhydramine and to bring a driver;\n- to stop metformin until we tell him to restart;\n- to check his blood sugar more often while on prednisone and off metformin;\n- to drink plenty of fluids and arrive by 8:45;\n- to tell imaging staff about the 2019 reaction, and which warning signs need emergency care.\n\nI also signed a chart note with all of this (doc-t0009).",
  "resumed": false,
